            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0566" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.1D1/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-11T19:00:00-05:00">October 11, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>120. Your 33, April 11, noon.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d239-f1"/> You are requested
                    to notify the Secretary General of the League of Nations in the sense of the
                    following, referring to his communication of April 10, 1929, addressed to the
                    Secretary of State: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Government of the United States, being desirous of cooperating in a
                            work which has for its object the proper treatment of foreigners, is
                            pleased to inform the Secretary General that it has designated George A.
                            Gordon, American First Secretary at Paris, to attend the Conference as a
                            technical expert to cooperate in a consultative capacity.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Please request Consul at Geneva to forward immediately to Gordon League documents
                    concerning the Conference including the draft Convention and any information
                    which he believes will be of assistance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
